  "_readme": [
    "Every SQL file in db/migrations and db/pending, and every migration recorded in the live supabase_migrations.schema_migrations, with how we know it is (or is not) applied.",
    "Checked by scripts/check-migrations.mjs (npm test). \"Absent from schema_migrations\" is NOT \"unapplied\": see provenance plain_sql.",
    "provenance: schema_migrations (applied by the migration tool; version given) | recovered (applied, file rebuilt from the live statement; body below the marker line must md5-match) | plain_sql (applied as ad-hoc SQL, no history row; evidence says how it was verified) | reconstructed (live objects that appear in no migration; definitions read back from the catalog).",
    "After applying anything: move the file from db/pending to db/migrations, record it here with its version (or evidence), and refresh schema_migrations with `node scripts/check-migrations.mjs --print-sql` (run via MCP) + `--live <saved output>`."
